   "name": "Items found in a traditional kitchen"
  }
 ],
 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "A traditional kitchen is usually a separate hut with a fireplace, using local materials and fuels.\nCommon items and their uses:\n• fireplace (three stones), firewood store;\n• clay pots: cooking and keeping water cool;\n• grinding stone: grinding pepper, egusi and spices;\n• mortar and pestle: pounding fufu, yams and cocoyams;\n• smoke rack above the fire: drying and smoking fish, meat and maize;\n• calabashes: serving drinks, storing grains;\n• charcoal pots and sawdust stoves: cooking with charcoal or sawdust;\n• wooden spoons and baskets.\nFuels: firewood, charcoal, sawdust, dried palm fronds and kernel shells.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {
   "k": 100
  },
  "problem": "Look at the drawing of a traditional kitchen. The part labelled {letterOf(k, 6, 1)} hangs above the fire. What is it and what is it used for?",
  "steps": [
   "It is the smoke rack.",
   "Fish, meat and maize placed on it are dried and preserved by the smoke and heat."
  ],
  "answer": "The smoke rack: for drying and smoking food.",
  "checks": [],
  "figure": "traditionalKitchen(k)"
 },
